  "content": "Putting is the clear team-wide priority. Every one of your seven players is losing strokes on the greens, all in a range from -2.16 to -3.92 strokes per round over their last 11-18 recorded rounds:\n\n| Player | SG Putting | Window |\n|---|---|---|\n| Owen Carter | -2.16 | 12 rounds |\n| Ethan Park | -2.72 | 13 rounds |\n| Mason Rivers | -3.00 | 12 rounds |\n| Dylan Brooks | -3.00 | 12 rounds |\n| Tyler Hayes | -3.34 | 11 rounds |\n| Jackson Hale | -3.91 | 15 rounds |\n| Cole Bennett | -3.92 | 18 rounds |\n\nBy contrast, the team is net positive off the tee (five of seven players between +0.81 and +1.35 SG-tee) and roughly break-even around the green. Approach play is the second-largest leak — everyone is negative there too, from -0.97 (Cole Bennett) to -3.83 (Owen Carter) — but putting is worse across the board and worse for more players.\n\nThree focus areas already target putting mechanics (Owen Carter's 5-10ft make rate, Cole Bennett's 3-5ft make rate, and 3-putt cascades for Jackson Hale, Cole Bennett, and Dylan Brooks), but Ethan Park, Mason Rivers, and Tyler Hayes have no active putting focus area despite being in the same negative range. Worth adding a putting-specific practice block for the whole team and closing that gap for those three.\n\n_Some figures in this answer could not be traced back to your program's data, so I've flagged it rather than presenting them as fact. Please ask again._",
